nswer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9452dea-0516-5dbe-b6c0-9467c07d8296" :question/math-academy-id "q-335021" :question/problem "![](images/2a/2aaa545dfada7732569ce6b813f32d050fa453aa83dc101495147d25330b7bc3.png)\n\nConsider the phase portrait above showing a solution of a Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=4x-2xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-9y+3xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x=x(t),y=y(t),$ and $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are positive constants.\n\nSelect the options below that best describe the dynamics of the system from point $A$ to point $B$ on the solution.\n\n$\\,$\nThe trajectory \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$\nThe number of prey {{field-3}} and the number of predators {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model is given by\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=ax-bxy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-cy+dxy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,d$ are positive real constants. Here, $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements:\n\n- The trajectory $\\text{circles around}$ $\\text{the nonzero equilibrium}.$\n\n- From $A$ to $B,$ the number of prey $\\text{decreases}$ and the number of predators $\\text{increases}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445108 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c9c2220-030e-5418-915c-e34d7962c077" :knowledge-point/title "Analyzing a Solution of the Lotka-Volterra Model Given the Phase Portrait"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e536196-5953-59fb-b1e9-7bde007287af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "decreases" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445013} {:answer/id #uuid "c6d7d5eb-2fb2-5cb2-8c07-015b23811f12" :answer/type 