} and the number of predators {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model is given by\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=-ax+bxy \\\\ {y}^{′}=cy-dxy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,d$ are positive real constants. Here, $x=x(t)$ represents the predators and $y=y(t)$ represents the prey.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements:\n\n- The trajectory $\\text{circles around}$ $\\text{the nonzero equilibrium}.$\n\n- From $A$ to $B,$ the number of prey $\\text{decreases}$ and the number of predators $\\text{increases}.$"}]}
